// CDLRICKSHAWMAN recognizes the Rickshaw Man pattern over bars startIdx through
// endIdx.
//
// Single-candle doji with two long shadows whose body sits near the midpoint of
// the high-low range. It is a neutral indecision signal, not a directional
// (bullish/bearish) reversal. A hit marks market indecision/uncertainty;
// neutral, neither bullish nor bearish.
//
// Formula and more info at https://ta-lib.org/functions/cdlrickshawman.
//
// Inputs, each at least endIdx+1 long:
//   - inOpen: Open price of each bar.
//   - inHigh: High price of each bar.
//   - inLow: Low price of each bar.
//   - inClose: Close price of each bar.
//
// Outputs, each at least as long as the values written (the input length always
// suffices):
//   - outInteger: +100 when the pattern is present, 0 otherwise. Never -100;
//     the positive value does not imply bullish, it signals uncertainty.
//
// Element k of each output is the value at bar BegIdx+k of the returned
// [OutRange], and BegIdx is at least [Core.CDLRICKSHAWMANLookback]: a range
// that ends before it returns NBElement 0.
//
